WEBVTT

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:08.613
She took it. There's no turning back.

00:00:08.973 --> 00:00:11.493
So how are we going
to get to Minnesota from here?

00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:12.613
Well, why don't we go down

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:14.613
to the elephant lot and rent an elephant?

00:00:14.693 --> 00:00:15.973
Hey. That sounds nice.

00:00:16.173 --> 00:00:17.573
We're taking the bus, nitwit!

00:00:19.773 --> 00:00:21.613
ANGER: There's a bus
leaving tomorrow. Perfect!

00:00:21.773 --> 00:00:23.813
A ticket costs money.
How do we get money?

00:00:24.213 --> 00:00:26.173
-Mom's purse.
-(GASPS) You wouldn't.

00:00:26.293 --> 00:00:29.013
Oh, but I would.
Where was it we saw it last?

00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:31.893
-♪ TripleDent gum ♪
-No!

00:00:32.013 --> 00:00:34.053
-(FEAR SCREAMS)
-It's downstairs somewhere.

00:00:34.373 --> 00:00:35.853
Mom and Dad got us into this mess.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.533
ANGER: They can pay to get us out.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.653
How about this, huh? Isn't this nice?

00:00:42.773 --> 00:00:44.653
You can see everything from up here.

00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:46.813
Look, there's Inductive Reasoning.

00:00:46.893 --> 00:00:48.013
There's Déjà Vu.

00:00:48.093 --> 00:00:49.453
There's Language Processing.

00:00:49.693 --> 00:00:50.853
There's Déjà Vu.

00:00:51.013 --> 00:00:52.173
There's Critical Thinking.

00:00:52.253 --> 00:00:53.493
There's Déjà Vu.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.333
Hey, look at this, guys! Memories!

00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:58.853
Hey. That was a good idea.

00:00:59.373 --> 00:01:01.213
About scaring Riley awake.

00:01:01.573 --> 00:01:02.653
JOY: You're not so bad.

00:01:03.053 --> 00:01:04.093
Really?

00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:05.733
Nice work.

00:01:06.893 --> 00:01:09.133
JOY: Oh, I can't wait
to get the old Riley back.

00:01:09.413 --> 00:01:10.453
As soon as we get there,

00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:11.973
I'm going to fix this whole mess.

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:13.573
Whoa. Is this Riley?

00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:16.493
She's so big now.
She won't fit in my rocket.

00:01:16.573 --> 00:01:17.893
How are we gonna get to the moon?

00:01:18.053 --> 00:01:20.653
Oh, it's that time
in the twisty tree, remember?

00:01:20.973 --> 00:01:22.493
The hockey team showed up

00:01:22.573 --> 00:01:24.613
and Mom and Dad were there cheering.

00:01:25.053 --> 00:01:27.373
JOY: Look at her,
having fun and laughing.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.653
Oh, I love this one.

00:01:29.893 --> 00:01:31.973
Hmm. I love that one, too.

00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:34.573
Atta girl! Now you're getting it!

00:01:34.653 --> 00:01:36.933
Yeah. It was the day the Prairie Dogs

00:01:37.053 --> 00:01:38.773
lost the big playoff game.

00:01:38.893 --> 00:01:40.573
Riley missed the winning shot.

00:01:40.693 --> 00:01:42.813
She felt awful. She wanted to quit.

00:01:44.653 --> 00:01:47.253
Sorry. I went sad again, didn't I?

00:01:48.293 --> 00:01:51.453
I'll tell you what. We can keep working
on that when we get back. Okay?

00:01:52.293 --> 00:01:53.373
Okay.

00:01:55.413 --> 00:01:56.693
MOM: But I just don't understand.

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:01.453
Why did our moving van
even go to Texas?

00:02:06.413 --> 00:02:07.693
Multiple customers?

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:17.093
Well, we were promised
delivery on the fifth.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.173
Uh-huh.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:30.493
Excuse me,
isn't there any way that you can rush it?

00:02:31.173 --> 00:02:32.453
(RUMBLING)

00:02:34.413 --> 00:02:35.413
(GASPS)

00:02:35.933 --> 00:02:37.053
JOY: Honesty Island?

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.813
(ALL SCREAMING)

00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:46.333
(GASPS) Look out!

00:02:52.973 --> 00:02:54.133
ENGINEER: Come on!

00:02:57.893 --> 00:02:59.533
-(ALL SCREAMING)
-Hold on!

00:03:00.253 --> 00:03:01.653
Hurry up! Come on! Over here!

00:03:01.813 --> 00:03:03.533
WORKER: Come on, people!
Let's, go, go, go!

00:03:15.853 --> 00:03:17.013
JOY: That was our way home.

00:03:17.653 --> 00:03:20.173
We lost another island?
What is happening?

00:03:20.293 --> 00:03:22.973
Haven't you heard?
Riley's running away.

00:03:23.693 --> 00:03:24.733
What?

00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:27.933
FEAR: Wait, wait, hang on, guys.

00:03:28.813 --> 00:03:30.013
Are we really doing this?

00:03:30.413 --> 00:03:31.933
-I mean, this is serious.
-Look.

00:03:32.013 --> 00:03:33.093
We have no Core Memories.

00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:34.733
ANGER: You want Riley to be happy?

00:03:34.853 --> 00:03:36.933
Let's get back to Minnesota
and make more.

00:03:38.533 --> 00:03:41.013
Joy, if we hurry, we can still stop her.

00:03:42.813 --> 00:03:44.173
Family Island. Let's go!

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:56.373
(RUMBLING)

00:03:58.373 --> 00:04:00.893
(GASPS) Joy! Joy!

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.053
SADNESS: It's too dangerous!

00:04:02.173 --> 00:04:03.893
-SADNESS: We won't make it in time.
-(THUDDING)

00:04:07.293 --> 00:04:08.573
But that's our only way back!

00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:09.813
(BOTH GRUNTING)

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.573
A recall tube!

00:04:25.293 --> 00:04:26.733
We can get recalled!

00:04:30.413 --> 00:04:32.133
MOM: Have a great day, sweetheart.

00:04:32.573 --> 00:04:34.373
See you after school, monkey.
(IMITATING MONKEY GRUNTING)

00:04:34.453 --> 00:04:35.533
We love you!

00:04:40.093 --> 00:04:41.253
Go! Run, run! Go!

00:04:51.853 --> 00:04:54.573
Whoa! Whoa! Sadness! Sadness, stop!

00:04:55.773 --> 00:04:56.933
You're hurting Riley!

00:04:57.013 --> 00:04:58.853
Oh, no, no, no! I did it again!

00:04:59.253 --> 00:05:00.453
If you get in here,

00:05:00.573 --> 00:05:02.733
these Core Memories will get sad.

00:05:03.613 --> 00:05:04.613
(RUMBLING)

00:05:08.493 --> 00:05:11.493
I'm sorry. Riley needs to be happy.

00:05:11.813 --> 00:05:12.973
Joy?

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:22.813
(GASPS)

00:05:23.293 --> 00:05:24.533
-(SCREAMING)
-(GASPS)

00:05:27.173 --> 00:05:28.773
Joy! (SCREAMING)

00:05:33.213 --> 00:05:34.213
Joy!

00:05:50.813 --> 00:05:51.933
(JOY GRUNTING)

00:06:00.813 --> 00:06:01.973
(GASPING)

00:06:06.853 --> 00:06:07.853
Joy?

00:06:12.893 --> 00:06:13.893
(GASPS)

00:06:14.933 --> 00:06:15.933
Joy!

00:06:20.933 --> 00:06:22.213
(GRUNTING)

00:06:22.653 --> 00:06:24.813
Joy, what are you doing?
Will you stop it, please?

00:06:26.213 --> 00:06:27.813
(JOY PANTING)

00:06:29.533 --> 00:06:32.533
Don't you get it, Joy?
We're stuck down here.

00:06:33.533 --> 00:06:34.613
We're forgotten.

00:06:42.893 --> 00:06:45.333
RILEY: We used to play tag and stuff.

00:06:49.613 --> 00:06:51.533
But everything's different now.

00:06:54.093 --> 00:06:55.333
Since we moved.

00:06:56.733 --> 00:06:57.853
(RILEY SNIFFLING)

00:07:03.373 --> 00:07:04.453
(SIGHS)

00:07:06.053 --> 00:07:07.173
(SNIFFLES)

00:07:08.413 --> 00:07:09.653
(RILEY LAUGHING)

00:07:15.013 --> 00:07:16.893
(RILEY TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

00:07:18.573 --> 00:07:19.773
(JOY SNIFFLING)

00:07:23.413 --> 00:07:24.733
(RILEY HUMMING)

00:07:26.573 --> 00:07:29.413
Do you remember how she used to

00:07:29.493 --> 00:07:31.933
stick her tongue out
when she was coloring?

00:07:41.773 --> 00:07:44.893
I could listen to her stories all day.

00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:52.453
(RILEY LAUGHING)

00:07:58.613 --> 00:08:01.213
I just wanted Riley to be happy.

00:08:04.453 --> 00:08:05.773
And now...

00:08:09.653 --> 00:08:11.133
(CRYING)

00:08:23.333 --> 00:08:24.533
(RILEY LAUGHING)

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:41.653
(KIDS CHEERING)

